Feature: Admin change notices
  A change to a table the admin shows tells the admin through the admin_changes channel, but a change that
  only keeps the books, such as a click count or a sync token, does not.

  Scenario Outline: A table tells the admin of a change, but not of bookkeeping
    Given the database runs "<before>"
    When the database runs "<change>" while the admin listens
    Then the admin hears of "<heard>"

    Examples:
      | case                         | before                                                                                                                                                              | change                                                                                                                       | heard               |
      | an insert                    |                                                                                                                                                                     | insert into tags (name, color, scope) values ('ruby', 'mk-blue', 'public')                                                   | tags                |
      | a change to another column   | insert into tags (name, color, scope) values ('ruby', 'mk-blue', 'public')                                                                                          | update tags set name = 'rails'                                                                                               | tags                |
      | only updated_at              | insert into tags (name, color, scope) values ('ruby', 'mk-blue', 'public')                                                                                          | update tags set updated_at = now()                                                                                           | nothing             |
      | a short link click           | insert into short_codes (code) values ('go-there'); insert into short_links (short_code_id, destination) select id, 'https://example.com' from short_codes          | update short_links set click_count = click_count + 1, last_clicked_at = now()                                                | nothing             |
      | a share download             | insert into short_codes (code) values ('one-file'); insert into share_group_files (short_code_id, key, filename, content_type, byte_size) select id, repeat('0', 32), 'a.txt', 'text/plain', 1 from short_codes | update share_group_files set download_count = download_count + 1                         | nothing             |
      | a share group view or zip    | insert into short_codes (code) values ('a-group-of'); insert into share_groups (short_code_id) select id from short_codes                                           | update share_groups set view_count = view_count + 1, zip_download_count = zip_download_count + 1                             | nothing             |
      | a client that was used       | insert into oauth_clients (client_id, visitor_hash, redirect_uris, grant_types, response_types) values ('client', repeat('0', 64), '{https://example.com}', '{authorization_code}', '{code}') | update oauth_clients set last_used_at = now()                                          | nothing             |
      | a new Gmail history id       | insert into mail_accounts (provider, name, history_id) values ('gmail', 'me', '1')                                                                                  | update mail_accounts set history_id = '2'                                                                                    | nothing             |
      | a Gmail settings sync        | insert into mail_accounts (provider, name) values ('gmail', 'me')                                                                                                   | update mail_accounts set settings_synced_at = now()                                                                          | nothing             |
      | a new signature              | insert into mail_accounts (provider, name) values ('gmail', 'me')                                                                                                   | update mail_accounts set signature = 'Aaron'                                                                                 | mail_accounts       |
      | a calendar sync token        | insert into calendars (account, google_id, name) values ('me@example.com', 'primary', 'Me')                                                                         | update calendars set sync_token = 'next', synced_from = current_date                                                         | nothing             |
      | a calendar name              | insert into calendars (account, google_id, name) values ('me@example.com', 'primary', 'Me')                                                                         | update calendars set name = 'Work'                                                                                           | calendars           |
      | renewed credentials          | insert into service_connections (provider, account_id, label, credentials) values ('google', 'me', 'Me', 'sealed')                                                  | update service_connections set credentials = 'renewed'                                                                       | nothing             |
      | a revoked connection         | insert into service_connections (provider, account_id, label, credentials) values ('google', 'me', 'Me', 'sealed')                                                  | update service_connections set revoked_at = now()                                                                            | service_connections |
      | a new lapse date             | insert into service_connections (provider, account_id, label, credentials) values ('google', 'me', 'Me', 'sealed')                                                  | update service_connections set lapses_at = now()                                                                             | service_connections |
      | a reconnect                  | insert into service_connections (provider, account_id, label, credentials, revoked_at) values ('google', 'me', 'Me', 'sealed', now())                               | update service_connections set credentials = 'renewed', revoked_at = null                                                    | service_connections |
      | a commit walk                |                                                                                                                                                                     | insert into sync_states (kind, sync, repo, synced_at) values ('backfill', 'commits', 'blog', now()); delete from sync_states | nothing             |
      | a failing sync               |                                                                                                                                                                     | insert into sync_states (kind, sync, repo, synced_at, failure_reason, failing_since) values ('failure', 'commits', 'blog', now(), 'boom', now()) | sync_states |
